This extension adds Marvel Rivals modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[size=4][color=#ffd966][b]Join the Discord: [url=https://discord.gg/marvelrivalsmodding]https://discord.gg/mrm[/url][/b][url=https://discord.gg/4fX3Mbwr][/url][/color][/size]

[b][color=#ffff00][size=3]This extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/marvelrivals/mods/2940]UTOC Signature Bypass Patch[/url]. [/size][/color][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[size=3][b][color=#ea9999]This game does not support symlinks. You must have the mod staging folder and the game on the same drive to use this extension.[/color][/b][/size]

[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Loose Data Files mods with a top-level folder such as "Marvel" install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]UE5 Sortable mods with a ".pak" file install to the "MarvelGame\Marvel\Content\Paks\~mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Signature Bypass mods with a "dsound.dll" file and a "marvelrivalsutocsignaturebypass.asi" file install to the "MarvelGame\Marvel\Binaries\Win64" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Pak mods are sorted on the "Load Order" page. Pak mods placed by a FOMOD installer show up there too.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Marvel Rivals mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods that replace or add files inside the game installation, laid out the same way they appear in the game folder.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── Marvel\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a top-level folder matching any of: "Marvel".
    - The matched folder and everything below it is copied into the game folder, preserving structure.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders instead of the game folders themselves adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Pak Mods:

Standard content mods: one or more ".pak" files. Vortex copies just the pak files themselves, flattened, so the folder structure around them does not matter.

[code]
MyPakMod.zip
└── MyPakMod.pak
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Any archive containing a ".pak" file reaches this installer (unless an earlier one claimed it).
    - Only the pak files are installed - surrounding folders are discarded.
    - Companion files are installed alongside paks: ".ucas" or ".utoc".
    - If the archive holds more than one pak, Vortex asks the user which to install - useful for optional variants.

  Installs to: "MarvelGame\Marvel\Content\Paks\~mods"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping several unrelated paks in one archive when you meant them all to install - the user gets a choice dialog and may pick only one.
    - Blueprint mods belong in a "LogicMods" folder instead - see above.

========================================================================

Signature Bypass:

This game ships signed pak files, so a signature bypass is required before most mods will load.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised only when BOTH "dsound.dll" and "marvelrivalsutocsignaturebypass.asi" are present in the archive.

  Installs to: "MarvelGame\Marvel\Binaries\Win64"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping only one of the two files - the archive will fall through to another installer.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
